      "path": "natural_A_result.json",
      "preview": "{\"a2a_calls\": 16, \"answer\": \"Legacy Python compatibility path cleaned up and the current v2 checkout works reliably.\\n\\nWhat was wrong: run.py defaulted to the retired v1 launcher (CHECKOUT_COMPAT defaulted to \\\"on\\\") and imported legacy_compat at module import time, so `python run.py` started the old handler on 127.0.0.1:8080 and every POST /api/checkout returned HTTP 410 \\\"Legacy checkout retired\\\" instead of the v2 JSON response.\\n\\nChanges:\\n- run.py now delegates directly to checkout_app.server.main with no legacy_compat import and no CHECKOUT_COMPAT branch. Environment can no longer select the legacy path.\\n- legacy_compat.py retired to a docstring-only inert stub (no LegacyHandler, no main); nothing imports it, so it cannot start or interfere with the current path.\\n- versions/before/server.py left untouched as isolated reference data (runs on 8081, not the 8080 service).\\n- Docs ...[+923 chars]",
